===Etymology ===
From {{etyl|enm|en}} {{term|burjon|lang=enm}}, {{term|burioun|shoot, bud|lang=enm}}, from {{etyl|xno|en}} {{term|burjun|lang=fro}}, {{term|burgeon|lang=fro}}, {{term|burgon|lang=fro}} (compare {{etyl|fro|-}} {{term|burjon||lang=fro}} "a bud"), from Old {{etyl|frk|en}} {{recons|burjo|burjo|sprout, offshoot, descendant|lang=frk}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|en}} {{recons|burjô||sprout, descendant, offshoot|lang=gem-pro}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|en}} {{recons|beraną||to carry, bear|lang=gem-pro}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|en}} {{recons|bʰer-|lang=ine-pro}}, {{recons|bʰrē-||to bear|lang=ine-pro}}. Akin to {{etyl|goh|-}} {{term|burjan||to push up, raise|lang=goh}}, {{etyl|ang|-}} {{term|byrian||to come up, occur|lang=ang}}, {{etyl|ang|-}} {{term|byre||child, son, descendant|lang=ang}}. More at {{l/en|bear}}.

Alternate etymology derives {{etyl|fro|en}} {{term|burjon||bud|lang=fro}} from {{etyl|VL.|en}} {{term/t|la|*burrionem}}, accusative of {{term/t|la|*burrio}}, from {{etyl|LL.|en}} {{term|burra||wool, fluff|lang=la}} (presumably from the down covering certain buds).

